From bf2ab30a16bb0122d1b37fae80efe443039af689 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:34:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the direct solvers of SuperLU_DIST and STRUMPACK

SuperLUSolver (src/SuperLUSolvers.cxx) wraps mfem::SuperLUSolver: the
matrix of hypre is copied when the operator is set, and given to the
solver of MFEM just before the resolution, so that the solver of MFEM
never holds an operator which is not factorized. The solver of MFEM is
built again when the global size changes. ReuseAnalysis keeps the column
permutation for the operators of the same sparsity pattern (SamePattern).
The parallel symbolic factorization (option ParallelSymbolicFactorization,
or the ParMETIS column permutation) is refused on one process and with
the reuse of the analysis, where SuperLU_DIST 9.2.1 crashes.

STRUMPACKSolver, STRUMPACKMixedPrecisionSolver (STRUMPACK >= 7) and the
STRUMPACKPreconditioner preconditioner (src/STRUMPACKSolvers.cxx) take
the options of STRUMPACK by its command line (Options parameter, a
boolean giving a flag), then the settings of mfem-mgis (tolerances,
verbosity, reuse of the reordering). The solver of MFEM is built again
when the global size changes. STRUMPACK reports a success when its
Krylov solver or its iterative refinement stops at the maximum number of
iterations: such a resolution is reported as not converged.
